# Give the usbpower relay controller a stable device name: /dev/usbpower
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS
#
# /dev/ttyACM0 is assigned in plug order, not per device. An Arduino Uno is a
# USB-CDC device, and so is a Pixhawk / PX4 / ArduPilot flight controller, a
# 3D printer board, and plenty of other hardware -- they all compete for
# ttyACM0, ttyACM1, ... depending on what was plugged in first.
#
# That is dangerous for a service that opens a port automatically at boot. If
# the relay controller's service were pointed at a bare /dev/ttyACM0 and a
# flight controller happened to claim that name, the service would open the
# flight controller's port, hold it open exclusively (so QGroundControl or
# MAVProxy could not connect), write relay commands into its MAVLink stream,
# and toggle DTR on open -- which resets many boards.
#
# This rule matches the relay controller by its unique USB serial number and
# creates /dev/usbpower, which always points at the right board no matter what
# else is plugged in or in what order. Point the service at /dev/usbpower
# instead of /dev/ttyACM0 and the collision cannot happen.
#
# ADAPTING THIS FOR A DIFFERENT BOARD
#
# Find your board's identifiers:
#
#     udevadm info -a -n /dev/ttyACM0 | grep -E 'idVendor|idProduct|serial'
#
# then substitute them below. Common values:
#
#     Arduino Uno R3 (genuine)     idVendor 2341  idProduct 0043
#     Arduino Nano (CH340 clone)   idVendor 1a86  idProduct 7523
#     Arduino Mega 2560            idVendor 2341  idProduct 0042
#
# CH340-based clones usually share one serial number across every unit (or
# report none at all), so ATTRS{serial} cannot distinguish two of them. For
# those, drop the serial match and use the physical port path instead
# (KERNELS=="1-2.4.1"), accepting that it pins the board to one USB socket.
#
# After editing:
#     sudo cp udev/99-usbpower-symlink.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#     sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger
#     ls -l /dev/usbpower

SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="2341", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0043", ATTRS{serial}=="55332333230351709192", SYMLINK+="usbpower", GROUP="dialout", MODE="0660"
